CORE
Test
--function Test.flags --max-nondet-string-length 20 --cp `../../../../scripts/format_classpath.sh . ../../../lib/java-models-library/target/core-models.jar ../../../lib/java-models-library/target/cprover-api.jar`
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
Test.class is compiled for Java 21 (javac --release 21), so only a runtime of Java 21 or later runs it: without --java-version, FormatFlagsConversionMismatchException names all the flags, as since Java 19. (The same with a class file of Java 8 is not proved, see StringFormatFloats/c6AnyBad and toString23AnyBad, and StringFormatErrors/flagsAnyBad.)
